note SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
note cqa.om: the DRA-184 coding agent runtime. One task = one directory DIR holding
note   issue.txt  the unfamiliar issue (free text, at most 8192 bytes)
note   own.txt    the files the agent may change, one repository-relative path per line (ownership)
note   test.txt   optional build/test command, one argv entry per line (absolute program path),
note              run with the working directory DIR/repo, 20 s limit, output captured
note   repo/      the isolated git worktree of the target repository at its pinned commit
note   journal.log  append-only, fsync'd checkpoint written by this program (format below)
note The agent loop: issue -> repository inspection (LIST, READ) -> patch (WRITE) -> build/test
note (TEST; also run after every WRITE) -> DONE. Inference is one POST /v1/chat/completions per
note step to 127.0.0.1:MPORT (the own Omega LLM, aien-train serve.om, DRA-119), temperature 0,
note seed 1. serve.om ignores `tools` ("this model never calls tools"), so the agent speaks a
note text protocol: the first line of the reply that starts with LIST, READ <path>,
note WRITE <path> (then one fenced block holding the whole new file), TEST or DONE is the action.
note No other model, provider or fallback exists in this program.
note
note Journal records, one line each, fields separated by one space, hex fields lowercase ("-" empty):
note   J 0 cqa1                          header
note   I s 0                             inference for step s started
note   R s pt ct ms hex(content)         its answer (prompt and completion tokens, wall ms)
note   N s reason status                 inference failed: reason 1 ctx, 2 http, 3 conn, 4 json
note   A s kind ok hex(path)             parsed action: kind 0 none, 1 LIST, 2 READ, 3 WRITE, 4 TEST,
note                                     5 DONE; ok 0 refused (bad path, not owned, no block)
note   E s hex(path)                     write intent (step s)
note   D s len fnv64                     write done: length and FNV-1a 64 of the new file
note   O s hex(observation)              what the agent was told after step s
note   X 0 0                             cancel request (appended by `cqa cancel`)
note   T 0 state                         terminal: 1 DONE, 2 CANCELLED, 3 BUDGET, 4 FAILED
note Recovery on every run: a torn last line is cut; a T ends the task; a step with R is never
note asked again (its answer is replayed into the history); an X before a step's E cancels it;
note an E without D repeats the idempotent full-file write (temporary file + rename) once.
note
note Commands:
note   cqa task DIR MPORT [steps=N] [maxtok=N] [crash=R|E|W]   run or resume; prints CQA lines
note   cqa cancel DIR                                         append X
note   cqa serve PORT MPORT WORK [steps=N] [maxtok=N] [max=K] endpoint for the frozen DRA-124
note        suite runner (accept.om): each POST /v1/chat/completions carrying a DRA-124 coding item
note        becomes task WORK/<k> (files from the prompt, git commit, owned = the named target),
note        runs the agent loop, and answers with the target file in one python block; a
note        context failure is answered 400 context_length_exceeded like serve.om.
note crash=R|E|W (tests only): exit 77 right after the first R, after the first E, or after the
note first file write before its D.
note Compose: { printf 'om2\n'; cat vendor/json.om vendor/jsonw.om vendor/http.om vendor/notls.om
note   ../runtime_path/rpcom.om cqa.om; } | omc > cqa   (tests/coding_qual/build.sh)

const GDIR ulong 0
const GP ulong 1024
const GP2 ulong 2560
const GISS ulong 4096
const GOWN ulong 12288
const GTST ulong 16384
const GACT ulong 20480
const GJB ulong 65536
const GJCAP ulong 1048576
const GOBS ulong 1114112
const GCON ulong 1179648
const GFIL ulong 1245184
const GFCAP ulong 262144
const GN ulong 1507328
const OBSCAP ulong 3000
const FILCAP ulong 3000

const VDL ulong 0
const VMP ulong 1
const VSTP ulong 2
const VMAXT ulong 3
const VCRSH ulong 4
const VISS ulong 5
const VOWN ulong 6
const VTST ulong 7
const VJL ulong 8
const VCON ulong 9
const VOBS ulong 10
const VKIND ulong 11
const VOK ulong 12
const VAPL ulong 13
const VWS ulong 14
const VWL ulong 15
const VPT ulong 16
const VCT ulong 17
const VMS ulong 18
const VRSN ulong 19
const VHST ulong 20
const VTERM ulong 21
const VSTEP ulong 22
const VMXP ulong 23
const VMXC ulong 24
const VTMS ulong 25
const VRL ulong 26
const VFL ulong 27
const VMAX ulong 28
const VK ulong 29
const VNC ulong 40
const VN0 ulong 41
const GWRK ulong 24576

